45. The Minister may make Tegulations for any of the
following purposes—

(a) to define the duties and powers of an Inspector of
Pawnbrokers;

(b) to regulate the tendering for and the granting of
licences;

\

(Pt. VII, S. 45-49)

PAWNBROKERS                            21

(c) to regulate the conduct|of the business of pawn-
broking by licensees;

(d) to regulate the pawning of articles by pawners;

(e) to prescribe forms of books to be used by licensees;

(f) to fix fees for licences;

(g) to prescribe on matters|stated or required in this
Act to be prescribed; and

(h) generally to give effect to the provisions of this Act.
